{
  "id": "COMPOUND:1169 - DISEASE:1932",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between desflurane and Macrostomia, mediated through the coiled-coil domain containing 33 (CCD33) protein. Desflurane, a volatile anesthetic, is shown to affect CCD33, which in turn is associated with multiple conditions, including Melanoma-Pancreatic cancer syndrome and Hypophosphatemic rickets, X-linked dominant. These conditions are all linked to CCD33 through a causal pathway, and CCD33 is directly implicated in causing Macrostomia. The scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship, with the highest scores in paths 1 and 2, suggesting a robust association. The mechanism appears to involve CCD33 as a central mediator, where desflurane's effects on CCD33 lead to the development of Macrostomia. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction between desflurane and CCD33 remains to be fully elucidated.",
